  "userDescription": "Ontology context for the modeled Furusato business vocabulary, selected entity keys and declared relationships. Use it to understand connectivity, paths, neighbourhood, membership and containment across Prefecture, Municipality, Donor, Gift, GiftCategory, Supplier, Donation and the pre-aggregated metric entities. Resolve entity IDs from the Lakehouse before traversing by name; reverse traversal uses `<-Relationship-`, and there is no direct Supplier-to-Donor edge. These declarations are schema/context, not executed-instance evidence, and do not by themselves prove binding or queryability. Treat `IncomingDonationAmountYen` as unavailable unless its binding and runtime are verified from current evidence. Claim graph traversal or GQL results only when actual GQL execution and returned results are available; for other native SQL/KQL/DAX results, identify the actual language and source and preserve query/result evidence. If a user explicitly requests GQL, do not silently substitute another language. Eventhouse KQL remains the operational-observation authority; use Lakehouse for complete attributes and data.",
